  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A genealogical tome bound in eternal ice-pages, spanning two flipper-spans when open. Created during **The Great Thaw**, the era of colonial expansion that followed the retreat of the great ice sheets, the Crystalline Lineage records every family constellation of Aurora Stack's founding bloodlines in aurora-ink that glows faintly when held by Aurora-descended penguins. It was discovered at **the Veil Vents**, a geothermal cluster in the Berg's remote reaches, wrapped in oilcloth predating living memory within the mineral crust of the third fissure.
    
    No account explains how it arrived there.
    
    ## Chain of Custody and Degradation
    
    The tome's history is best understood as a sequence of losses.
    
    | Holder | Damage Sustained |
    |---|---|
    | **Grandmother Deep**, eldest orca matriarch and Wake-Singer advisor | Three pages cracked by her teeth-marks; three additional pages missing from the spine entirely |
    | **Keeper Hollows**, hermit survivor of the Drowned Ledge flooding | Corruption from his tainted contact burned the aurora-ink black along the spine — the Drowned Ledge's influence, per Frost-ward Xumaijang's archival registry |
    | Proximity to **Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius**, a desecrated Nightshelf tunnel | Final three genealogies' ink burned irreversibly black |
    | **Light-Regent Lianoshing** (frost-born) mingi'Ward, Aurora Stack regent and veteran of the Faction Wars | Sealed the tome with her own fading aurora-light — a restorative act that diminished her permanently. Lianoshing died with her flippers resting on the cover |
    
    Accord judiciary interrogation of **Noctisius~**, a Nightshelf citizen detained for unlawful transfer of the tome, established that Grandmother Deep's acquisition was not opportunistic theft but deliberate reconnaissance into Aurora Stack bloodline records. The case was escalated to Glaciarch level. The three missing pages were never recovered.
    
    ## Current Status
    
    Recovered by Accord authorities after Lianoshing's death and secured in an evidence vault, ownership contested between Aurora Stack and parties unnamed in official filings. At last archival inspection, the remaining genealogies were barely legible — the tome requires active aurora exposure for recharging, which no one has authorized or, perhaps, thought to provide.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771574880359_0", anchor: "Grandmother Deep's acquisition was not opportunistic theft but deliberate reconnaissance into Aurora Stack bloodline records", text: "Reconnaissance. Into bloodline records. By the matriarch who advises the Wake-Singers — the cult that conducts blood-rituals of accumulated sacrifice to wake a dead god. The Accord judiciary established this finding and apparently saw no reason to ask the next question. I noted in my ☽'scar Ramtatus~ annotation that her presence there was recorded as 'residency' because the sources were terrified of the alternative. Here the alternative is plain: she was reading which families carried what aurora-light properties, and she was doing it for theological reasons. Bloodline is not a metaphor in Wake-Singer practice.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574880359_1", anchor: "the tome requires active aurora exposure for recharging, which no one has authorized or, perhaps, thought to provide", text: "Every founding family of Aurora Stack. Their constellations, their lineages, their names. Dying in an evidence vault because authorization requires a signature and no one whose job it is to sign things considers a genealogy urgent. I know what this looks like. I have watched it from the inside.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574880359_2", anchor: "Three pages cracked by her teeth-marks; three additional pages missing from the spine entirely", text: "Three cracked, three missing, three burned black. The symmetry should trouble the reader. Damage to ice-bound texts is not neat. Either the losses were systematic and deliberate — which reframes every stage of this chain of custody — or the sources are rounding to a pleasing number, which is worse, because it means we do not actually know how much is gone.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
